The meaning I want is "happening before the natural/expected start", i.e.
the counterpart of {za'o}. If all I wanted to say is that the event has
started, them {co'a} works perfectly.

> For the event which has started we have "ba'o pu'o"

This doesn't work, as I show with the falling ball example.

> and for the event which
> has been completed "ba'o mo'u".

That works, but this is not the meaning I'm interested in.

> A lot of the problems with "already" is that
