> immediately used as the counter-example.

The first is no solution.

> So,
>     .i mi ba'opu'o klama
>     I am already going.  (The going has started and is continuing).

Or "I was about to go but I decided not to". (The anticipated going
was not realized, and it is no longer anticipated.)

>     .i mi ba'omo'u klama
>     I have already gone.  (The going has been completed and is no longer
